---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-redvars-loader</code> is the Redvars r mark as a loading indicator, for the brand moment
  such as the first load of an app. Inside a page, use <code>wc-circular-progress</code> or
  <code>wc-linear-progress</code> instead. It is a <code>progressbar</code> named by
  <code>label</code> ("Loading" by default). It plays its full animation by default: that is the
  point of the loader.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2rem; align-items: center;'>
    <wc-redvars-loader></wc-redvars-loader>
    <wc-redvars-loader variant='trace'></wc-redvars-loader>
    <wc-redvars-loader variant='fill'></wc-redvars-loader>
    <wc-redvars-loader variant='pulse'></wc-redvars-loader>
    <wc-redvars-loader variant='orbit'></wc-redvars-loader>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Variants</h3>
<p>
  <code>variant</code> picks how the mark moves: <code>build</code> (the default: the stem rises
  and the arm swings out), <code>trace</code> (the outline draws itself and fills),
  <code>fill</code> (the r fills from the bottom), <code>pulse</code> (the tile beats and sends out
  a ring) or <code>orbit</code> (a runner chases round the tile).
</p>

<h3>Progress</h3>
<p>
  With <code>value</code> (0 to 100) the loader stops looping and fills the r to that level, and
  reports it with <code>aria-valuenow</code>.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-redvars-loader id='redvars-loader-progress' value='0' label='Installing'></wc-redvars-loader>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var loader = document.getElementById('redvars-loader-progress');
      var value = 0;
      setInterval(function () {
        value = value >= 100 ? 0 : value + 10;
        loader.value = value;
      }, 600);
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Size, color and motion</h3>
<p>
  <code>--redvars-loader-size</code> sets the edge (4rem by default),
  <code>--redvars-loader-tile-color</code> and <code>--redvars-loader-mark-color</code> the colors,
  and <code>--redvars-loader-duration</code> the length of one loop. Add
  <code>respect-reduced-motion</code> to follow the system's reduced-motion setting (on Windows,
  "Animation effects" turned off): every variant then becomes a slow fill of the r with nothing
  moving.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-redvars-loader
    variant='orbit'
    style='--redvars-loader-size: 6rem; --redvars-loader-duration: 3s;'
  ></wc-redvars-loader>
</DemoComponentCard>
